into one replace_text spanning from `def format` down through `_setup_logger`? That region includes formatTime and _root_logger etc. — about 40 lines. Actually I could do one replace_text covering the whole NewLineFormatter+setup region (lines 35-100), that's fine as a single replacement.\n\nSo:\nA: environ factory insert; stats edit.\nB: environ config insert; logger big block replace (formatter class through _setup_logger).\n\nThen run pytest, then artifacts (run.log, patch.diff). Wait — task requires run.log and patch.diff in start dir? The harness handles artifacts presumably. Task says \"在启动目录生成 run.log 和包含三个文件的完整 patch.diff\". Course harness likely generates these. I'll check task_status/plan requirements later; focus on code + pytest.\n\nLet me write A now.\n\nFor environ factory insertion, target text:\n\n```\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n```\n\nnew: append after it the new factory.\n\nFor stats:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n```\n→\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n```\nNeed uniqueness — \"logger.info(m)\" likely unique.\n\nLet me check the exact indentation from evidence: 12 spaces for `for m in msgs:`? The evidence snippet shows `    def _log_worker(...)` at col 0 and inside `for msgs in iter(q.get, None):` then `try:` then `if need_sleep:` ... `for m in msgs:` then `logger.info(m)`. The snippet lines: \"            for m in msgs:\" (12 spaces) and \"                logger.info(m)\" (16 spaces). Use that."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10100,"completion_tokens":3262,"total_tokens":13362,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3005},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6004},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}